{
  "note": "L + P/2 sweep account checked run by run on all 92 eligible transports (post hoc, no fitted parameter).\n\nage_reuse_model.py compares the sweep value L + P/2 with the observed mean moving-decision age for the\n24 primary runs. Here the same comparison is made for every eligible transport: the primary campaign,\nthe slow-update pilot, the exploratory campaign and the initial capture-proxy pilot. P is the median\nstart-to-start interval and L the mean capture-proxy-to-inference-end latency of the evidence bundles\nconsumed by the run's carry decisions, as in duty_cycle.analyse_run; the observed value is the mean\nlogged age over decisions whose mode is not 'stop', as in the run-level audit. A policy that moves\nregardless of evidence age is expected to lie near L + P/2; the age-aware rule departs from it when\nits score hold refuses motion on old evidence, which happens only when P + L exceeds the hold onset.\nThe sets are summarized separately and are not pooled into a matched comparison.\n",
  "runs_analysed": 92,
